In article <NN86302.91Jan10152046@kaarne.tut.fi> nn86302@tut.fi (Niilo Neuvo) writes:
>Yes if your AC is below zero, then your AC will be anything between your AC
>and zero. This determined randomly after each hit (I assume).
>
>Or that is at least what I was told.

Absolutely correct.  If your AC is below zero, the code will actually use
an AC that is a random AC between zero and your listed AC.  This can be
found in the mattacku() function in src/mhitu.c for those of you who are
interested.  Also, though, if you have an AC of -n, the damage that a
monster does to you will be reduce 1-n points, so go for those negative
AC values!

